@design/delegation-service.sigil from DelegationService import { delegation }
@design/task-core.sigil from TaskCore import {
  task, task id, child run, result, transcript, launch spec,
}
@design/agent-config.sigil from AgentConfig import {
  project root, unknown agent error, load error,
}
@design/pi-driver.sigil from PiDriver import {
  attach command, child session,
}
@design/task-store.sigil from TaskStore import {
  task record, task status, parent session id,
}

component Cli {
  goal {
    Give a person at a terminal the same delegation as the MCP server, plus a way
    to open and export what a child did after the parent session is gone.
  }

  logic {
    Every command starts through the delegation service, so that the
    start-up sweep runs first. On subzero run, make a delegation from the agent
    name and the brief in the arguments, with no parent session id, wait for it
    and print the result. When the agent name is unknown, print the
    unknown agent error to stderr and exit non-zero with no task made. When the
    agent file fails to load, print the load error to stderr and exit non-zero
    the same way. On subzero tasks, read the task records and print the id,
    agent, task status and creation time of every task. On subzero attach, read
    the launch spec of the task, refuse when the task has no recorded
    launch spec or its child run is live, and otherwise start the
    attach command. On subzero show, export the child session of the task as
    HTML with pi --export, and say that an abandoned task has no result. Each
    command ends by printing its output and exiting.
  }

  constraints {
    The Cli passes its working directory to the delegation service as its
    fallback project root, and the project root comes from AgentConfig in the
    order its constraints give.

    A delegation from the Cli must carry no parent session id, because a command
    line has no conversation.

    The attach command must be refused while the task status of the task is
    running, because the start-up sweep has already marked the task of a dead
    owner abandoned. It must also be refused with a message that no launch spec
    was recorded when the task record has none.

    Cli depends on DelegationService for the delegation, on TaskStore for the
    task record, on TaskCore for the launch spec and on PiDriver for the
    attach command.
  }

  cases {
    Attach on a task whose task status is running is refused. On a settled task
    it builds the attach command from the launch spec, and on a task with no
    recorded launch spec it is refused.

    Subzero run against a scripted pi writes the task record with task.json,
    events.jsonl and turns/1.json, appends an index line and prints the result.

    Subzero run with an unknown agent name prints the unknown agent error and exits
    non-zero without making a task.
  }

  interface {
    Offer four commands: subzero run with an agent and a brief, subzero tasks,
    subzero attach with a task id, and subzero show with a task id.

    Make the child session of a task, its transcript and its task record reachable
    by task id after the parent session has ended.
  }
}
